From 0efcba6eea0eb71c2f1cc762b65efdb6e194f216 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Liu <kwliu@nuvoton.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:49:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: class: obmf: flush the Bulk IN endpoint when a write
 fails

When the host stops polling the Bulk IN endpoint (for example while the
host driver is unbound), the write times out with the packet still in the
endpoint FIFO. Later writes then fail too, and the host cannot complete
discovery after it returns until SMC1 is reset. Flush the endpoint on a
failed write so the next message starts with an empty FIFO.

Reference: OCP OBMF Spec 1.0.0, Section 5.15 (OBMF-ICP Control Channel -
Channel 0)

Signed-off-by: Joseph Liu <kwliu@nuvoton.com>
---
 subsys/usb/class/obmf.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/subsys/usb/class/obmf.c b/subsys/usb/class/obmf.c
index 6def734e6de..68bef200a97 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/class/obmf.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/class/obmf.c
@@ -247,6 +247,8 @@ int obmf_usb_ep_write(const struct device *dev, const uint8_t *data,
 				(uint8_t *)data, data_len, USB_TRANS_WRITE);
 	if (ret != data_len) {
 		LOG_ERR("Transfer failure");
+		/* The host stopped polling: drop the packet left in the FIFO */
+		usb_dc_ep_flush(cfg->endpoint[0].ep_addr);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
